From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 06:18:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 023/260] [ae-patch] Fix the review findings on the Tabler
 project icons and the merge card

Post-merge review of https://github.com/analyticendeavors/omnigent-ae/pull/43
(patch 0015) and https://github.com/analyticendeavors/omnigent-ae/pull/53
(patches 0021 and 0022).

- useAeTablerIcons subscribes to the loader, so every icon that saw a failed
  load redraws once any later load succeeds (the picker's Try again).
- aeTablerIconData fetches the two JSON files as assets through an eager
  ?url glob instead of import(), and a retry adds retry=N to the URL: Safari
  caches a failed dynamic import, so retrying the same import() never worked.
- Icon lookups check own keys (Object.hasOwn), so tabler:constructor draws the
  folder instead of throwing and taking the Sidebar down.
- PROJECT_ICON_MAX_LENGTH goes from 16 to 48, which covers the longest
  tabler: value in @tabler/icons 3.46 (41 characters).
- Enter in an empty icon search picks nothing, so the landing tile no longer
  saves the first suggestion over the current icon.
- The icon picker focuses its search box on open, so the rename popover's
  auto-focus no longer lands on Remove icon.
- The inline PR card has a set width (w-xl, capped at the bubble), so the
  chat's w-fit bubble cannot shrink it to the message text.
- The merge method segments are disabled while the merge is pending.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
